          <caption>
            <p>Anatomy of the Human Visual Pathway.&#x000a0;This diagram illustrates the neurological route from the retina to the cortex of the occipital lobes, including the optic nerve, optic chiasma, and optic tract.&#x000a0;The image highlights the distribution of crossed and uncrossed fibers as they pass through landmarks like the commissure of Gudden, the lateral geniculate body, the pulvinar, and the superior colliculus. Additionally, the illustration identifies associated structures such as the medial geniculate body and the nuclei of the oculomotor, trochlear, and abducent nerves. Illustrated&#x000a0;by K Humphreys</p>
          </caption>
          <graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="VisualPathway2" position="float" orientation="portrait"/>
        </fig>
